   "slug": "selection-sort",
   "title": "Selection Sort",
   "level": 1,
   "statement": "<p>Sort a list of whole numbers from smallest to largest, this time with <strong>selection sort</strong>: find the smallest number among those not yet placed, swap it into the first unplaced position, and repeat.</p><p>(Again the judge only checks the output, but write the selection sort yourself.)</p>",
   "input": "<p>The first line holds <code>n</code>. The second line holds <code>n</code> integers.</p>",
   "output": "<p>The <code>n</code> integers in ascending order, separated by single spaces.</p>",
   "constraints": "<p>1 ≤ n ≤ 1000; 0 ≤ every number ≤ 10<sup>9</sup>.</p>",
   "examples": [
    {
     "in": "5\n1 4 2 3 5\n",
     "out": "1 2 3 4 5\n"
    }
   ],
   "hint": "<p>For each position <code>i</code>, keep the index <code>m</code> of the smallest number seen so far in <code>a[i:]</code>. When the inner loop ends, swap <code>a[i]</code> and <code>a[m]</code>.</p>",
   "solution": "n = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\nfor i in range(n - 1):\n    m = i\n    for j in range(i + 1, n):\n        if a[j] < a[m]:\n            m = j\n    a[i], a[m] = a[m], a[i]\nprint(*a)",
   "explanation": "",
