   "hint": "<p>Sort first. With <code>n</code> numbers, which index is the middle one? Try it for <code>n = 1</code>, 3 and 5.</p>",
   "solution": "n = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\nfor i in range(n - 1):\n    m = i\n    for j in range(i + 1, n):\n        if a[j] < a[m]:\n            m = j\n    a[i], a[m] = a[m], a[i]\nprint(a[n // 2])",
