   "hint": "<p>Either sort the evens and the odds as two separate lists and glue them together, or use one bubble sort where \"<code>x</code> should come after <code>y</code>\" means: <code>x</code> is odd and <code>y</code> is even, or they are both the same kind and <code>x &gt; y</code>.</p>",
   "solution": "def after(x, y):\n    if x % 2 != y % 2:\n        return x % 2 == 1\n    return x > y\n\n\nn = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\nfor i in range(n - 1):\n    for j in range(n - 1 - i):\n        if after(a[j], a[j + 1]):\n            a[j], a[j + 1] = a[j + 1], a[j]\nprint(*a)",
