   "slug": "zigzag-order",
   "title": "Biggest, Smallest, Biggest, Smallest",
   "level": 2,
   "statement": "<p>Print the numbers in a zig-zag order: first the largest, then the smallest, then the second largest, then the second smallest, and so on, until every number has been printed exactly once. Repeated values are separate numbers.</p>",
   "input": "<p>The first line holds <code>n</code>. Each of the next <code>n</code> lines holds one integer.</p>",
   "output": "<p><code>n</code> lines, one number per line, in the zig-zag order.</p>",
   "constraints": "<p>1 ≤ n ≤ 1000; −10<sup>9</sup> ≤ every number ≤ 10<sup>9</sup>.</p>",
   "examples": [
    {
     "in": "5\n10\n-1\n3\n3\n-9\n",
     "out": "10\n-9\n3\n-1\n3\n",
     "why": "Sorted: −9 −1 3 3 10. Take from the right end, then the left end, and keep alternating."
    }
   ],
   "hint": "<p>Sort the list, then keep two positions: one at the right end and one at the left end. Print from the right, move it in, print from the left, move it in, until they cross.</p>",
   "solution": "n = int(input())\na = [int(input()) for _ in range(n)]\nfor i in range(n - 1):\n    for j in range(n - 1 - i):\n        if a[j] > a[j + 1]:\n            a[j], a[j + 1] = a[j + 1], a[j]\nlo, hi = 0, n - 1\ntake_big = True\nwhile lo <= hi:\n    if take_big:\n        print(a[hi])\n        hi -= 1\n    else:\n        print(a[lo])\n        lo += 1\n    take_big = not take_big",
   "explanation": "",
