   "slug": "fair-team",
   "title": "The Fairest Team",
   "level": 3,
   "statement": "<p>A coach must pick <code>k</code> of the <code>n</code> players for a team. To keep the team even, the difference between the tallest and the shortest chosen player should be as small as possible. Print that smallest possible difference.</p>",
   "input": "<p>The first line holds <code>n</code> and <code>k</code>. The second line holds the <code>n</code> heights.</p>",
   "output": "<p>The smallest possible difference between the tallest and the shortest of <code>k</code> chosen players.</p>",
   "constraints": "<p>1 ≤ k ≤ n ≤ 1000; 1 ≤ every height ≤ 10<sup>9</sup>.</p>",
   "examples": [
    {
     "in": "7 3\n10 100 300 200 1000 20 30\n",
     "out": "20\n",
     "why": "Choose 10, 20 and 30."
    }
   ],
   "hint": "<p>In the sorted list, a best team is always <code>k</code> players standing next to each other. Why would you ever skip someone in between?</p>",
   "solution": "n, k = map(int, input().split())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\nfor i in range(n - 1):\n    m = i\n    for j in range(i + 1, n):\n        if a[j] < a[m]:\n            m = j\n    a[i], a[m] = a[m], a[i]\nbest = a[k - 1] - a[0]\nfor i in range(1, n - k + 1):\n    best = min(best, a[i + k - 1] - a[i])\nprint(best)",
   "explanation": "",
